This indicator measures the amount of water produced by PUB that is available for consumption by residential customers (litres per capita per day) after deductions are made due to water losses and non-residential consumption. Its increase illustrates both the increase in water production capacity and the reduction in non-revenue water.

MTR Assessment

The Betio desalination plant is likely to be commissioned by early 2025, and Mc Kenzie plant by end 2024. The PMU, Project Impementation Assistance consultant and the PUB are discussing strategies to put the additional water produced, to use through the existing water network - even though the new network is not yet ready. Once the water produced in desalination plants flows through&nbsp;the existing water network, this indicator will be updated.&nbsp;

However, the per capita quantum of water supplied including the baseline will have to be reassessed by the PMU, based on the water quantity produced and supplied to the people of South Tarawa currently (from the water reserve) and by the end of the project.

&nbsp;

